                    "body": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/@williamgaoharvard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"\u003e@williamgaoharvard\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;This hits a real problem for me. I'm building client sites all day (Next.js/Vercel stack), and half my best fixes come from randomly looking at someone else's live site mid-browsing, a layout choice, a hover state, whatever. By the time I'd switch over to the actual project and explain what I saw, the idea's already lost half its detail. Being able to just flag it right there and have the agent pick up the right project context is the actual unlock, not another AI sidebar. Curious how it handles multiple active client projects though, does it get the right one reliably when you've got a dozen repos open, or do you still have to nudge it toward the right context sometimes?\u003c/p\u003e",
